Package: selectiveHotelling
Title: Selective Hotelling T-squared Testing After Clustering with
    Unknown Covariance
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Yiqun", "Chen", , "yiqun.t.chen@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Selective p-values for testing whether two clusters estimated from
    the data have different means, when the covariance matrix of the features is
    unknown. The tests use the polar decomposition of the tested observations and
    an exact Monte Carlo construction (Besag and Clifford, 1989), and they apply
    to any clustering algorithm, including k-means and hierarchical clustering.
